# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Raw licensed research datasets — never commit these; each requires
# agreeing to its own licence and downloading from the original authors.
#   DaiSEE:     https://people.iith.ac.in/vineethnb/resources/daisee/
#   WESAD:      https://ubicomp.eti.uni-siegen.de/home/datasets/icmi18/
#   UBFC-Phys:  requested from the dataset authors
# fer2013 is the removed emotion branch's dataset (see README "Documented
# negative results") - unused, and large. feature_traces_BEFORE_calibfix is a
# stale local snapshot kept only as a personal diff reference.
#
# datasets/feature_traces/ and datasets/rppg_traces/ are deliberately NOT
# listed here: they are per-frame signal traces WE derived from UBFC-Phys
# videos, not the videos themselves. Per the recording protocol, each video
# is processed once and then deleted - these traces are the only remaining
# record of that processing, so they must be committed or that work is
# unrecoverable if the video can't be re-downloaded.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
datasets/DaiSEE/
datasets/WESAD/
datasets/UBFC-Phys/
datasets/processed_daisee/
datasets/fer2013/
datasets/feature_traces_BEFORE_calibfix/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Trained model binaries (21 MB + 29 MB) ARE tracked, but via Git LFS — see
# .gitattributes. LFS stores them outside normal git history, so cloning does
# not drag every past version along. They represent hours of training and can
# only be regenerated with the full 33 GB dataset, so they must be backed up.
#   Regenerate with: cd code && python train_daisee_stress.py
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
models/*.keras
models/*.tflite

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Personal session data — real recordings of a named individual's stress
# levels over time. Keep out of any shared repo.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/sessions.db
**/sessions.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Virtual environments
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/

# Streamlit (the app's own .streamlit/ lives under code/, so match at any depth)
.streamlit/secrets.toml
**/.streamlit/secrets.toml

# Hosted-mode credentials. The Supabase PUBLIC key is not secret, but keep every
# env file out of git anyway; the service_role key must never be in this repo.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
supabase/.temp/
*.pem

# OS / editor noise
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Claude Code tool state (dev-server launch config, agent worktrees) - not
# project source
.claude/

# Scratch
*.log
tmp/
scratch/

# Training venv (PyTorch, kept separate from the TF stack)
.venv-train/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local-only "Auto-detect context" assets (code/context_detector.py): the
# Places365 scene model and the small environment test-image collection.
# Downloaded/derived files stay out of git (and out of the Docker image, which
# copies only code/ and models/); the docs describing their sources stay in.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
local_models/**
!local_models/**/
!local_models/**/SOURCES.md
!local_models/**/manifest.csv
# Converted context-detection models (models/context/): too large for plain Git,
# but copied into the Docker image by `COPY models`. Only the README is tracked.
models/context/**
!models/context/
!models/context/README.md
